WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.200
A new client sells to big retailers, but runs on a web store and a small inventory app. No NetSuite, so no Suite App.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:17.175
Something still has to pick up each eight fifty, create the store order, and send the ship notice and invoice back. That's an integration platform.

00:00:17.175 --> 00:00:26.025
Think of it as plumbing with a control room. Pipes connect systems, valves decide when things flow, and the control room shows every run.

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:33.600
We use two. Workato runs many existing integrations, which we maintain. New builds now go to StackSync.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:41.100
In Workato, one automation is a recipe. It reads like a short story: when this happens, do this, then this.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:47.250
The trigger starts it. A polling trigger asks every few minutes: anything new since last time?

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:56.700
Actions are the steps: search, create, update, or run some code. Datapills carry fields, like the P O number, from one step into the next.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:04.000
Each run of a recipe is a job. A job keeps the input and output of every step. This is where you debug.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:11.025
Open the failed step. Read what it got, and what came back. Then walk back to the step that made the bad input.

00:01:11.025 --> 00:01:19.375
Decide if it is a data, mapping, or connection problem. Fix it in the right place, and check the result in the destination system.

00:01:19.375 --> 00:01:28.025
A trap: after you click Repeat job, the old page still shows the old error. The new run is a new row at the top of the jobs list.

00:01:28.025 --> 00:01:36.025
StackSync works in a similar way. A workflow is a chain of modules, with a trigger, usually a schedule, and an on off switch.

00:01:36.025 --> 00:01:43.700
Credentials live in connections, shared settings live in workspace variables, and past runs are in the Log Explorer.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:52.750
Lessons learned the hard way. A schedule trigger made in the YAML editor looked right, but never fired. Create triggers in the designer.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:59.875
The run panel can say Processing long after a run finished. Verify by side effects and the Log Explorer.

00:01:59.875 --> 00:02:06.000
New workflows are created switched on. Switch them off straight away, then turn them on on purpose.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:14.925
Design every flow to be safe to re-run. For example, tag each order with its P O number, and skip any P O that already has one.

00:02:14.925 --> 00:02:22.550
Never let errors pass silently, and keep test and live separate: separate connections, separate workflows, clear names.

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:31.125
Remember: Workato is recipes, triggers, datapills, and jobs. StackSync is workflows, modules, and the Log Explorer.

00:02:31.125 --> 00:02:35.650
That completes the platforms track. Next: onboarding a client.

